mmit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2021-06-25T04:27:09Z","label":{"name":"TF 2.5","color":"5319e7"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/comments/869142741","html_url":"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/50445#issuecomment-869142741","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/50445","id":869142741,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg2OTE0Mjc0MQ==","user":{"login":"rodenkew","id":85350198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MzUwMTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85350198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew","html_url":"https://github.com/rodenkew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-27T11:00:12Z","updated_at":"2021-06-27T11:00:12Z","body":"We considered using SELECT_TF_OPS, but the increase in the size of the resulting binary makes this option very unattractive.\r\n\r\nThe fact that the converter produces an artifact that the interpreter cannot run definitely seems like an issue with one or both products. The fact that the TfLite 1.15 converter/interpreter pair did not have this problem seems like a regression.\r\n\r\nGiven that the concatenation kernel and the split_v kernel support kTfLiteInt64, it is surprising that the split kernel does not. After comparing the the split and split_v kernels, I think that the behavior described in this ticket seems almost trivial to address.\r\n\r\nIn fact, I made the obvious (but maybe incorrect) update to split.cc, built from source, and the issue was resolved.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/comments/869142741/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"rodenkew","id":85350198,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MzUwMTk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85350198?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew","html_url":"https://github.com/rodenkew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rodenkew/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/comments/869257650","html_url":"https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/50445#issuecomment-869257650","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tensorflow/tensorflow/issues/50445","id":869257650,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg2OTI1NzY1MA==","user":{"login":"abattery","id":3203059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3203059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com